IMPORT prelude

-- Parliament (Privileges, Immunities and Powers) Act 1962 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for an ordinary person, a publisher, a
-- witness or a Member: freedom of speech and the Member's immunity (ss 5, 6, 20(2), (3)), protection of Parliamentary publications
-- (ss 7, 8), exemption from service and arrest (ss 9 to 11), summonses and warrants (ss 13, 25, 26), witnesses (ss 15 to 17, 31(m)),
-- Parliament's punitive powers (ss 20, 21(2), 22(2)), the suspended Member's salary (s 29(3)), the offences and their penalties
-- (ss 31, 35, 36), the bar on prosecution without referral (s 37), and the death gratuity for a Member (s 11A(1), (2)(a), (3)(a), (6)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (page footer: "version in force from 9/3/2025"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/PPIPA1962.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021
-- and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". Later amendments are annotated in the body: [Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022] on
-- s 7(1), and [Act 5 of 2025 wef 09/03/2025] on ss 34 and 40, the latest annotated.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. This is REQ-0139 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the provisions such a person meets. Not encoded: s 3 (the privileges of the UK House of Commons at the
-- establishment of the Republic, which are imported wholesale and not set out), ss 4, 12, 14, 18, 19, 23, 24, 27, 28, 30 (Parliament's
-- and the Speaker's powers beyond their effect on the person), s 16(1), (3) (the President's affairs-of-State certificate), ss 32 to 34
-- beyond their penalty, ss 38 to 40, and in s 11A the office-holder's commuted sum and paragraphs (2)(b) to (d) and (3)(b) to (e)
-- other than (3)(e)'s amount. The Standing Orders and the Parliamentary Pensions Act 1978 were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the writing-l4-rules conventions as the example rows show them. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Parliament (Privileges, Immunities and Powers) Act 1962`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the higher of` MEANS IF `a` GREATER THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `5, 6, 20(2), (3) -- freedom of speech and the Member's immunity`

-- s 5: freedom of speech and debate and proceedings in Parliament "shall not be liable to be impeached or questioned in any court ...
-- or any other place whatsoever out of Parliament".
-- s 6(1): "No Member shall be liable to any civil or criminal proceedings, arrest, imprisonment or damages by reason of any matter or
-- thing which he may have brought before Parliament or a committee ... or may have said in Parliament or in committee."
-- s 20(2): a Member "found guilty of abuse of privilege in respect of anything said in Parliament by him" may by resolution be
-- suspended "from the privileges and immunities conferred by sections 3, 5 and 6 insofar as they relate to liability to civil
-- proceedings"; (3) during that period he "shall be liable to civil proceedings in respect of anything said by him in, or any written
-- statement made by him to, Parliament". The suspension reaches civil proceedings only: criminal immunity stays.
GIVEN `said or brought before Parliament or a committee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the proceedings are civil` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `immunity suspended by resolution under s 20(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Member is immune from the proceedings` IF
        `said or brought before Parliament or a committee`
    AND NOT (`the proceedings are civil` AND `immunity suspended by resolution under s 20(2)`)

-- s 6(2): "No person shall be liable ... by reason of any act done under the authority of Parliament or the Speaker and within its or
-- his legal powers or under any warrant issued by virtue of those powers."
GIVEN `done under the authority of Parliament or the Speaker` IS A BOOLEAN, `within legal powers or under a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person acting for Parliament is protected` IF
    `done under the authority of Parliament or the Speaker` AND `within legal powers or under a warrant`

§§ `7, 8 -- protection of Parliamentary publications`

-- s 7(1): a defendant in civil or criminal proceedings for publishing, by himself or his employee, "by order or under the authority of
-- Parliament or any committee", any reports, papers or journals, may "on giving to the claimant or prosecutor ... 24 hours' written
-- notice of his intention", bring before the court a certificate "under the hand of the Speaker or of the Clerk" stating that the
-- publication was so authorised. (2): "The court shall thereupon immediately stay the civil or criminal proceedings", and they are
-- "deemed to be finally determined".
GIVEN `published by order or under the authority of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `hours of written notice given` IS A NUMBER,
      `certificate of the Speaker or the Clerk produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must stay the proceedings` IF
        `published by order or under the authority of Parliament`
    AND `hours of written notice given` AT LEAST 24
    AND `certificate of the Speaker or the Clerk produced`

-- s 8: in proceedings "for printing or publishing any extract from or abstract of any report, paper or journal as in section 7
-- mentioned, if the court is satisfied that the extract or abstract was printed or published bona fide and without malice, judgment
-- shall be entered for the defendant or accused".
GIVEN `an extract or abstract of an authorised report` IS A BOOLEAN, `bona fide and without malice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `judgment must be entered for the defendant` IF
    `an extract or abstract of an authorised report` AND `bona fide and without malice`

§§ `9 to 11 -- exemption from service, arrest and process`

-- s 9(1): it is not lawful "(a) to require any Member or officer of Parliament to serve as an assessor on any tribunal; or (b) while in
-- attendance on Parliament or any committee, to compel such person to attend as a witness in any court or tribunal" or inquiry.
GIVEN `a Member or officer of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN, `in attendance on Parliament or a committee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be compelled to attend court as a witness` IF
    NOT (`a Member or officer of Parliament` AND `in attendance on Parliament or a committee`)

-- s 10: "Except for a contravention of this Act, no Member shall be liable to arrest, detention or molestation in respect of any matter
-- which may be the subject of any civil proceedings while proceeding to, or in attendance at, or returning from, any sitting".
GIVEN `going to, attending or returning from a sitting` IS A BOOLEAN, `for a contravention of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Member may be arrested on a civil matter` IF
    (NOT `going to, attending or returning from a sitting`) OR `for a contravention of this Act`

-- s 11: "except in respect of a contravention of this Act, no civil or criminal process may be served or executed -- (a) in Parliament
-- or in the precincts thereof while Parliament is sitting; or (b) in any room in Parliament while a committee is sitting therein."
DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `the precincts while Parliament is sitting`
    `a committee room while the committee is sitting`
    `the precincts while Parliament is not sitting`
    `a private home`

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place, `in respect of a contravention of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `process may be served there` IF
        `in respect of a contravention of this Act`
    OR  CONSIDER `the place`
        WHEN `the precincts while Parliament is sitting` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a committee room while the committee is sitting` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `13, 25, 26 -- summonses and warrants`

-- s 13(3) (and s 25(3) in the same words): the summons "shall be served on the person ... either by delivering to him a copy thereof or
-- by leaving a copy thereof at his usual or last known place of abode in Singapore with some adult person". (4): by an officer of
-- Parliament or a police officer.
DECLARE Service IS ONE OF
    `a copy delivered to him`
    `a copy left at his home with an adult`
    `a copy left at his home with a child`
    `a copy left in his letterbox`
    `a copy sent by email`

GIVEN `the service` IS A Service, `served by an officer of Parliament or a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the summons is duly served` IF
        `served by an officer of Parliament or a police officer`
    AND CONSIDER `the service`
        WHEN `a copy delivered to him` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a copy left at his home with an adult` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 26(1): "If a person to whom a summons under section 13 or 25 is directed does not attend at the time and place mentioned therein,
-- the Speaker may, upon being satisfied that the summons was duly served, issue a warrant to apprehend him".
GIVEN `the service` IS A Service, `served by an officer of Parliament or a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `attended as summoned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Speaker may issue a warrant to apprehend` IF
        (NOT `attended as summoned`)
    AND `the summons is duly served` `the service` `served by an officer of Parliament or a police officer`

§§ `15 to 17, 31(m) -- witnesses`

-- s 31(m): no person shall "refuse to be examined before or to answer any lawful or relevant question put by or to produce any paper
-- ... required by Parliament or any committee unless the refusal is based on privilege or is excused". s 16(2): a person summoned has
-- "the same privilege as before a court of law". s 15: an objection that the matter "is of a private nature and does not affect the
-- subject of inquiry" may be excused by the Speaker or chairman, or reported to Parliament.
GIVEN `the question is lawful or relevant` IS A BOOLEAN, `the refusal is based on privilege` IS A BOOLEAN, `the refusal is excused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing to answer is an offence` IF
        `the question is lawful or relevant`
    AND (NOT `the refusal is based on privilege`)
    AND (NOT `the refusal is excused`)

-- s 17(1): "no person who gives evidence before Parliament or any committee shall be liable to any civil or criminal proceedings ... by
-- reason of anything which he may have said in such evidence"; (2) no such statement "shall be admissible in evidence against that
-- person in any civil or criminal proceedings"; (3) except proceedings "for an offence under section 191 of the Penal Code 1871 or for
-- any offence under this Act in respect of any evidence given by him".
DECLARE Proceedings IS ONE OF
    `a defamation suit`
    `a prosecution for an unrelated crime`
    `a prosecution for false evidence under s 191 of the Penal Code`
    `a prosecution for an offence under this Act about the evidence`

GIVEN `the proceedings` IS A Proceedings
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the witness's evidence can be used against him` IF
    CONSIDER `the proceedings`
    WHEN `a prosecution for false evidence under s 191 of the Penal Code` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a prosecution for an offence under this Act about the evidence` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `20, 21(2), 22(2) -- Parliament's punishments`

-- s 20(1): for "dishonourable conduct, abuse of privilege or contempt" by a Member, Parliament may (a) commit him to prison "for a term
-- not extending beyond the current session"; (b) fine him "not exceeding the sum of $50,000"; (c) suspend him from the service of
-- Parliament; (d) direct that he be reprimanded or admonished "in his place" by the Speaker.
-- s 20(4): for contempt by a stranger: (a) prison as above; (b) a fine not exceeding $50,000; (c) "exclude him from Parliament and the
-- precincts thereof"; (d) reprimand or admonition "at the Bar of the House".
-- s 21(2): on a select committee's report, Parliament may inflict the s 20 punishments "and also in the case of a Member expel him".
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `a Member`
    `a stranger`

DECLARE Punishment IS ONE OF
    `imprisonment until the end of the session`
    `a fine`
    `suspension from the service of Parliament`
    `exclusion from Parliament and its precincts`
    `reprimand in his place`
    `reprimand at the Bar of the House`
    `expulsion`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the punishment` IS A Punishment, `on the report of a select committee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Parliament may impose the punishment` IF
    CONSIDER `the punishment`
    WHEN `imprisonment until the end of the session` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a fine` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `suspension from the service of Parliament` THEN `the person` EQUALS `a Member`
    WHEN `reprimand in his place` THEN `the person` EQUALS `a Member`
    WHEN `exclusion from Parliament and its precincts` THEN `the person` EQUALS `a stranger`
    WHEN `reprimand at the Bar of the House` THEN `the person` EQUALS `a stranger`
    WHEN `expulsion` THEN (`the person` EQUALS `a Member`) AND `on the report of a select committee`

GIVEN `the fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fine is within Parliament's power` IF `the fine` AT MOST 50000

-- s 22(2): "In the event of the prorogation or dissolution of Parliament, Parliament shall not take cognizance of any offence committed
-- by a Member unless complaint thereof has been lodged by way of motion or reference to a committee within 21 days of the date of the
-- commencement of the next Parliament."
GIVEN `days after the next Parliament commenced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Parliament may take cognizance of the Member's earlier offence` IF
    `days after the next Parliament commenced` AT MOST 21

-- s 29(3): "No salary or allowance payable to such Member for his service as a Member of Parliament shall be paid in respect of any
-- period during which he is suspended from the service of Parliament."
GIVEN `months suspended` IS A NUMBER, `monthly salary and allowances` IS A NUMBER, `months in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Member's pay for the period` MEANS
    (`months in the period` MINUS `months suspended`) TIMES `monthly salary and allowances`

§§ `31, 35, 36, 37 -- offences and penalties`

-- s 36(1): a contravention is an offence punishable "(a) for a contravention of section 35, [by] a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ...
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding 7 years or ... both; (b) for a contravention of section 31(d), (o), (p) or (q), [by] a fine not
-- exceeding $7,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or ... both; and (c) for a contravention of any other provision
-- of this Act, [by] a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or ... both".
-- s 36(2): an attempt or abetment carries "the penalty to which he would have been liable for a contravention of the provision itself".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `bribing a Member under s 35`
    `a Member accepting a bribe under s 35`
    `compelling a Member by force or menace under s 31(d)`
    `presenting a falsified document under s 31(o)`
    `tampering with a witness under s 31(p)`
    `a wilful false answer under s 31(q)`
    `ignoring a summons under s 31(b)`
    `defaming a Member over his conduct in Parliament under s 31(g)`
    `publishing committee evidence before its report under s 31(i)`
    `creating a disturbance under s 31(l)`
    `a Member voting despite a pecuniary interest under s 32`
    `publishing a false copy of an Act under s 34`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `bribing a Member under s 35` THEN 10000
    WHEN `a Member accepting a bribe under s 35` THEN 10000
    WHEN `compelling a Member by force or menace under s 31(d)` THEN 7000
    WHEN `presenting a falsified document under s 31(o)` THEN 7000
    WHEN `tampering with a witness under s 31(p)` THEN 7000
    WHEN `a wilful false answer under s 31(q)` THEN 7000
    OTHERWISE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `bribing a Member under s 35` THEN 7
    WHEN `a Member accepting a bribe under s 35` THEN 7
    WHEN `compelling a Member by force or menace under s 31(d)` THEN 3
    WHEN `presenting a falsified document under s 31(o)` THEN 3
    WHEN `tampering with a witness under s 31(p)` THEN 3
    WHEN `a wilful false answer under s 31(q)` THEN 3
    OTHERWISE 2

-- s 35(3): on conviction under s 35 "the court shall in addition to any penalty ... order that the value of the fee, gift ... or other
-- advantage, which is the subject of the offence, shall be paid by the recipient into the Consolidated Fund".
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `value of the advantage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the recipient must pay into the Consolidated Fund` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `bribing a Member under s 35` THEN `value of the advantage`
    WHEN `a Member accepting a bribe under s 35` THEN `value of the advantage`
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 37: "No prosecution shall be instituted in any court for an offence under this Act unless the matter giving rise to that
-- prosecution has been referred to the Public Prosecutor under section 21(1)." s 21(1)(c): Parliament may so refer "if the offence is
-- an offence mentioned in Part 5".
GIVEN `referred to the Public Prosecutor by Parliament under s 21(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution may be instituted` IF `referred to the Public Prosecutor by Parliament under s 21(1)`

§§ `11A -- death gratuity for a Member`

-- s 11A(1): where "at any time after 20 May 2011 -- (a) a Member dies while serving as a Member; or (b) a Member, having opted under
-- section 7 of the Parliamentary Pensions Act 1978 to receive a full pension without any gratuity, dies within one year of his pension
-- taking effect", there "may be paid" to dependants as the President thinks fit, or to his legal personal representatives, a death
-- gratuity. (8): "no person shall have an absolute right to any death gratuity". "Within one year" is read here as within 12 whole
-- months of the pension taking effect (an encoding choice; the text counts no days). The 20 May 2011 date is not modelled.
GIVEN `died while serving as a Member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `opted for a full pension without gratuity` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months from pension taking effect to death` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a death gratuity may be paid` IF
        `died while serving as a Member`
    OR  (`opted for a full pension without gratuity` AND `months from pension taking effect to death` AT MOST 12)

-- s 11A(2): the amounts are given for "a pensionable Member who has 9 or more years of reckonable service as a Member". "Reckonable
-- service" (subsection (6)) is service "on and after 3 June 1959 but not after 20 May 2011".
GIVEN `completed years of reckonable service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11A(2) gives the pensionable Member an amount` IF `completed years of reckonable service` AT LEAST 9

-- s 11A(6): "Member's commuted sum" means "a capital sum ascertained by multiplying the commutation factor of 175.14 by the lower of
-- ... (a) two-thirds (2/3) of his annual salary as a Member; (b) ... in respect of every completed year of reckonable service,
-- one-thirtieth (1/30) part of his annual salary; and ... in respect of any remaining uncompleted year ... one-three-hundred and
-- sixtieth (1/360) part of his annual salary for each completed month". "Annual salary" is "the annual equivalent of the highest
-- monthly rate of salary received by the Member during any period of his reckonable service". The factor multiplies an ANNUAL amount
-- as the text is written; that is encoded literally (see NOTES.md finding 1).
GIVEN `highest monthly salary` IS A NUMBER, `completed years` IS A NUMBER, `further completed months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Member's commuted sum` MEANS
    175.14 TIMES (`the lower of` `two-thirds` `the accrual`)
    WHERE
        `annual salary` MEANS `highest monthly salary` TIMES 12
        `two-thirds` MEANS `annual salary` TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 3
        `the accrual` MEANS `annual salary` TIMES `completed years` DIVIDED BY 30 PLUS `annual salary` TIMES `further completed months` DIVIDED BY 360

-- s 11A(2)(a): a pensionable Member who never held office (or held it before, not at death, with less than 8 years as an office-holder)
-- receives "an amount equal to one of the following sums, whichever is the higher: (i) the annual equivalent of the monthly rate of
-- salary received by him as a Member immediately before his death; (ii) the Member's commuted sum". "Monthly rate of salary" excludes
-- the non-pensionable allowances.
GIVEN `last monthly salary` IS A NUMBER, `highest monthly salary` IS A NUMBER, `completed years` IS A NUMBER, `further completed months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pensionable Member's death gratuity without office` MEANS
    `the higher of` (`last monthly salary` TIMES 12) (`the Member's commuted sum` `highest monthly salary` `completed years` `further completed months`)

-- s 11A(3)(a): a non-pensionable Member who "has never held any office" receives "an amount equal to the annual equivalent of the
-- monthly rate of salary received by him as a Member immediately before his death". (3)(e) gives the same amount to a former
-- office-holder with less than 8 years as one. No minimum service is stated for non-pensionable Members.
GIVEN `last monthly salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the non-pensionable Member's death gratuity without office` MEANS `last monthly salary` TIMES 12
